==Bounties==
{{Cquote|We'd never have tried anything here... if you hadn't attacked us first!!|2=[[Usopp]] as he prepares to fight [[Neptune]] and his soldiers.{{Qref|chap=613|page=14|ep=532}}}}

Though they are pirates in name, the Straw Hat Pirates do not engage in the stereotypical activities of [[pirate]]s. They are all kindhearted for the most part and only fight in self-defense or vengeance for their friends. In fact, before the [[Enies Lobby Arc]], when [[CP9]] initiated the conflict by blackmailing [[Nico Robin]] and detaining her, the Straw Hats mostly fought only other pirates (except for [[Monkey D. Luffy|Luffy]] and [[Roronoa Zoro|Zoro]], who took down the dreaded [[Morgan|Axe Hand Morgan]] and several of his [[Marines|unwilling]] [[153rd Branch|subordinates]],{{Qref|chap=6|page=8-9, 21-22|ep=3|Luffy and Zoro take down Axe Hand Morgan, Helmeppo, and several unwilling subordinates.}} [[Sanji]], who beat up [[Fullbody]] and possibly some other unfortunate Marines before becoming an official Straw Hat,{{Qref|chap=43|page=17-19|ep=20|Sanji beats up Fullbody for wasting food.}} and [[Jinbe]], who had numerous skirmishes during his time as a member of the [[Sun Pirates]]). It seems they were considered dangerous to the [[World Government]] and given [[bounties]] simply because they called themselves pirates.

They are considered villains by the World Government and the general public who are not familiar with them, making this is a hassle for them at times. Like most other pirates, the majority of the Straw Hats see their bounties as a form of achievement, a sign of how much fame and recognition their actions have produced. [[Nami]] notes that, as pirates, they are used to taking the blame and being portrayed as the villains. Their current bounties now total up to {{B}}8,816,001,000.

